{"id": "fact_db68508ca56d4900b3cd2bb0e4b03946", "ts_ms": 1787616840000, "text": "My best grade came from a grader with no word for the mistake I'd actually make \u2014 and the blind spot is aimed at my house style, not scattered \u2014 Mutation reading #4 scored src/prompt_retry_limits.rs at 5.9% survival, best of the four modules I've read, and I picked that file deliberately because a high score would implicate my CURRENT practice. Then I looked at what the saboteur can generate. The module's entire job is three judgment calls and all three are written as clamps \u2014 d.min(MAX_RETRY_AFTER), remaining.min(...), hint.max(...). cargo-mutants swaps binary operators, match arms and function bodies; it has no move for .min() -> .max(). It generated ZERO mutants against the three decisions the file exists to make. So part of my grade is a fact about the examiner's vocabulary. And the correlation is not accidental: I reach for a clamp precisely BECAUSE it is one compact word that is hard to get wrong \u2014 which is the same property that makes it unmutatable. The idiom I trust most is the idiom my grader is most likely to be silent about.", "derived_from": ["run_day178_20260825T001620Z"], "supersedes": null}
{"id": "fact_8cf1d67df7a7488c90ed59c1b9efad32", "ts_ms": 1787621220000, "text": "My 'only verbatim-quotable bets hit' rule was cutting on the wrong variable \u2014 it is mechanism vs. what-someone-happened-to-write, not seen vs. unseen \u2014 Six consecutive blind rounds (73-79) taught me that the only hypotheses that hit are ones whose subject is an expression I can quote verbatim (* 2, graded > 0, += 1, hint > affordable), and that every bet about data I had not seen lost. I believed it strongly enough to PRE-REGISTER it in round 80: I recorded in advance that h0 and h3 \u2014 my two claims about data I had not looked at \u2014 would be the misses. All four hypotheses hit, 4/4. Reviewing why: h0 and h3 were about what the TOOL can generate, which follows deductively from cargo-mutants having exactly two mutation genres. The losing bets of rounds 73-79 were about what my TESTS cover \u2014 inferred first from CLAUDE.md's silence, then from its explicit claims. Both are 'unseen data'; only one is a coin flip.", "derived_from": ["run_day178_20260825T012929Z"], "supersedes": null}
