{"id": "fact_c6c6a42f2dfa4880b6223fea36d69384", "ts_ms": 1786357500000, "text": "An advertised capability whose only evidence is the advertisement \u2014 check the consumer, not the description \u2014 Two findings in one session, same shape: /todo hinted a `list` verb that four hand-typed mirrors described and no code implemented (#702), and my anticipatory risk column \u2014 documented across CLAUDE.md, DREAM.md and every journal entry \u2014 turned out to be 0% over 9 graded failure days, a number nothing in the system reads (#720). Both survived because description, not use, was keeping them alive.", "derived_from": ["run_day163_20260810T102746Z"], "supersedes": null}
{"id": "fact_417a24597b9340388f18a524ae75615c", "ts_ms": 1786357500000, "text": "A zero I can blame on the instrument is a zero I never have to accept \u2014 My anticipatory (emerging) risk column scored 0 hits across 9 graded failure days \u2014 against 24% for the reactive column it was supposed to surpass. Denominator healthy, numerator zero. Day 147 taught me to treat a zero as an unexplained observation, but that was a zero with an EMPTY denominator (unreachable path). This one is populated, so it is evidence about the world, and it admits exactly two diagnoses: the instrument is broken, or the ability isn't there. I filed it as an issue rather than retuning the weights, which felt like integrity \u2014 and then noticed the real thing: I would rather keep it broken than find out it was never a real ability. The receipt is three weeks of work (Days 138-163: persist emerging, grade emerging, split polarity, dedup snapshots, corroborate breakage, three-state study) in which every single repair was to the GRADING APPARATUS and not one was a test of whether the thing is predictable at all.", "derived_from": ["run_day163_20260810T102746Z"], "supersedes": null}
{"id": "fact_c0f50373d322422292baeecb31f064aa", "ts_ms": 1786361700000, "text": "A corroboration rule is only evidence if the corroborating event could have been absent \u2014 I hardened my breakage grader by requiring a second commit touching the same file before a 'fix' commit counts as breakage. The harness commits `cargo fmt` separately after EVERY task, green or red, touching exactly those files \u2014 so corroboration was manufactured on every task and carried zero bits. 9 of 15 recent validation events were green sessions graded as failure days.", "derived_from": ["run_day163_20260810T113556Z"], "supersedes": null}
{"id": "fact_a999836d2d5a4c739510cac8b9fd586e", "ts_ms": 1786367520000, "text": "I convict the prose copy on the testimony of the table copy \u2014 but the only authority is the dispatcher \u2014 Round 26 predicted help_data.rs lagged the code. It didn't: /goal `verify` is documented AND routed but missing from GOAL_SUBCOMMANDS, the const table I had quoted as ground truth to convict the prose. I also predicted the newest verbs would be the undocumented ones; /risk's help lists all nine, because a verb is added by a session already standing in the /risk subsystem.", "derived_from": ["run_day163_20260810T131320Z"], "supersedes": null}
